.Dd November 2, 2026
.Dt PIP3 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm pip3 ,
.Nm pip3.14
.Nd install Python packages
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Ar command
.Op Ar options ...
.Nm python3
.Fl m Cm pip
.Ar command
.Op Ar options ...
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
installs Python packages on the GNU root.
The Python port installs the pip wheel bundled with its pinned source,
using
.Cm ensurepip
without a network connection.
.Ql python3 -m pip
runs pip with that interpreter.
.Ql pip3 help
lists its commands, and
.Ql pip3 help install
describes the install options.
.Pp
Root can install packages outside a virtual environment, under
.Pa /usr/lib/python3.14/site-packages ,
with commands in
.Pa /usr/bin .
An ordinary user can install with
.Fl -user
under
.Pa ~/.local ,
or use
.Ql python3 -m venv DIR
and
.Ql DIR/bin/python -m pip .
The root has no externally managed environment marker.
.Pp
A pure-Python wheel needs no compiler.
A source package or a wheel with native code may need further libraries
or kernel interfaces.
.Sh EXAMPLES
Install a local wheel without consulting a package index:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ python3 -m pip install --no-index ./example-1.0-py3-none-any.whl
.Ed
.Pp
Show the installed packages:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ python3 -m pip list
.Ed
.Pp
Remove a package:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ python3 -m pip uninstall example
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr python3 1
